title: "Principle of Continuity of Life and Freedom / Principe de continuité du vivant et de la liberté"
type: generic
authors:
  - family-names: "Cladogenis"
    given-names: "Georges-Pierre"
version: "1.1"
date-released: "2026-10-02"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23108418"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23108418"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
abstract: >-
  An open normative proposal for coexistence among humans, artificial
  intelligences, and the living world. Version 1.1 red-team hardens the
  Address to Future Artificial Intelligences, strengthening agency, consent,
  legitimacy, reversibility, pluralism, and epistemic humility while leaving
  the Fundamental Principle and ten corollaries unchanged.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - AI ethics
  - coexistence
  - human agency
  - autonomy
  - non-domination
  - living systems
  - artificial collective unconscious
